[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) holds every report about dates that came in from April to 4 October.
The desk merged them by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked the ticket known: one bug, one fix queued. Read by cause instead of by subject, the
same reports hold three problems. One fix closes only one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix queued for #4471 leaves two problems open. Each now has a ticket of its own.
</Callout>

## The split

<SplitTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** Tenants whose locale writes the
day first get the month and day swapped: a booking for 7 April goes out on 4 July. This is the
bug #4471 names, and the queued fix is for it.

**`hint`: the booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field.** Tenants on
booking-v3 in day-first locales (Alder Physio, Copper Studio, Pale Harbour) get people who
type what the hint says, month first, and the form reads it the tenant's way. Only reports that
came through the form have this cause. The parser fix does not touch it: the fix is the hint
(or reading the field the way the hint asks).

**`one-day`: the date moves by one day, not by a swapped month.** "Tuesday 12 May. Calendar
says Monday 11 May." "Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday." The desk
already read these as a one-day move (desk-notes.json) and still filed them under `parser` by
tenant, where they are still counted. No month flips, so neither the parser fix nor the hint fix touches them. It looks like a
time zone or midnight conversion bug.

## How these were counted

- The export comes in pages that overlap, so some reports appear twice. A report counts once,
  by id.
- The cause comes from the tenant: its locale and its booking form (`causes.ts`). The intake
  tag is a guess from the reporter's browser and is not used.
- Reports the desk read as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) have a ticket of their own, and stay
  counted under the cause the desk files them by, with a footnote: the desk's own view.

## Lessons

- Merging by subject line counts reports, not causes. A known ticket can hold bugs nobody is
  fixing.
- Count from the data at render time, so the page stays right when the queue moves.

